<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wang Ben</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">3rd century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wang Ben was a general of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/state-of-qin">State of Qin</a>, son of the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-jian-qin">Wang Jian</a>, active in the wars of unification under King Zheng. In 225 BCE he took the Wei capital Daliang by flooding it, and he then destroyed the last Yan forces in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaodong">Liaodong</a> and, in 221 BCE, occupied the State of Qi, completing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a>'s unification of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</p></div>
